  "limits": [
    "The meaning of the dirty latch is inferred from its concrete set/consume/value-update paths in this exact binary; it is not a documented CVI public ABI.",
    "No numeric text-child offset was introduced into production from this analysis; do not read arbitrary offsets or assume other CVI binaries match.",
    "Zero +0x44/+0x48 is evidence of no active native editor context, not an exhaustive memory-level proof that every widget record is clean. The latter would require additional verified widget traversal.",
    "No assertion about physical laser behavior is made. Application callbacks can issue parameter writes; the investigation concerns avoiding those callbacks.",
